WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:26.760
Whether you're a small business owner or you're just starting your first side hustle,

00:30.000 --> 00:51.240
if you're serious about scaling, your first hire shouldn't be a junior assistant or even

00:51.240 --> 00:52.340
a VA.

00:52.340 --> 00:59.860
You should actually think about hiring AI.

00:59.860 --> 01:06.400
It should actually be AI.

01:06.400 --> 01:09.500
I want you to start thinking of AI as your first hire.

01:09.500 --> 01:14.440
The reason being, it works 24-7 and it almost makes no mistakes.

01:14.440 --> 01:19.500
There are the occasional hallucinations here and there, but seriously, it doesn't complain,

01:19.500 --> 01:26.040
it doesn't take breaks and you don't have to explain it over and over and over.

01:26.040 --> 01:45.580
I want you to start thinking of AI as your first hire.

01:45.580 --> 01:54.120
I want you to start thinking of AI as your first hire.

01:54.120 --> 01:58.520
The reason being, it works 24-7 and it makes almost zero mistakes.

01:58.820 --> 02:01.280
It doesn't forget and it never complains.

02:01.540 --> 02:02.680
It doesn't even take breaks.

02:02.680 --> 02:10.220
The goal isn't to add more hours to your day.

02:10.220 --> 02:16.760
The goal is to buy back your time.

02:16.760 --> 02:18.300
The goal is to buy back your time.

02:18.300 --> 02:23.300
The goal is to buy back your time.

02:23.300 --> 02:28.840
So the more automations you have taking care of repetitive tasks, the more you can actually

02:28.840 --> 02:37.720
focus on the money making ones.

02:37.720 --> 02:42.800
The goal is to expand your capacity by connecting the dots, creating systems that talk to each

02:42.800 --> 02:59.260
other and that automate your workflow.

02:59.260 --> 03:02.900
Now once you've actually mapped out all of your workflows, you've started to create them

03:02.900 --> 03:24.940
and you actually start to have some synergy in your systems.

03:24.940 --> 03:29.860
Now once you've actually created all of your brand docs, all of your visual style guidelines

03:29.860 --> 03:35.460
and all of the documents you need to actually feed AI, you need to start thinking about expansion.

03:35.460 --> 03:37.360
So you're gone.

03:37.360 --> 03:40.440
So you've gone from chaos to clarity.

03:40.440 --> 03:52.240
This is the natural next step, expanding your systems, adding to them.

03:52.240 --> 03:58.060
This is where you start to link those one-off workflows together to create that synergy.

03:58.060 --> 04:02.620
If you have an onboarding system, that onboarding system can be connected to your email system.

04:02.620 --> 04:04.560
Your email system can actually...

04:04.560 --> 04:13.780
I don't want to do that.

04:13.780 --> 04:16.280
This is where you start linking your workflows together.

04:16.280 --> 04:21.280
This is where you let AI automate and connect all of the dots that you've actually been creating.

04:21.280 --> 04:42.280
This is where you're creating.

04:42.280 --> 04:47.740
It's about letting the automations and AI take over chunks of your work and buy back hours

04:47.740 --> 04:50.980
and hours of your time.

04:50.980 --> 04:56.180
It's about building leverage.

04:56.180 --> 05:06.680
It's about building leverage so that your efforts and your systems multiply.

05:06.680 --> 05:07.680
Think about it.

05:07.680 --> 05:16.140
What's holding most businesses back isn't talent.

05:16.140 --> 05:17.340
Think about it.

05:17.340 --> 05:20.140
What's holding most businesses back, it's not talent.

05:20.140 --> 05:21.500
It's time.

05:21.500 --> 05:27.680
Everybody wants more time in their day.

05:27.680 --> 05:41.140
Most owners are stuck in that manual 90% repetitive task mode.

05:41.140 --> 05:53.140
They're just...

05:53.140 --> 05:55.600
Most are stuck in that manual mode.

05:55.600 --> 05:56.600
Every lead.

05:56.600 --> 05:57.600
Every email.

05:57.600 --> 05:58.600
Every phone call.

05:58.600 --> 05:59.600
Every missed voicemail.

05:59.600 --> 06:00.600
Every contract.

06:00.600 --> 06:03.100
Every proposal that has to be sent out.

06:03.100 --> 06:08.100
It has to be done on a repetitive basis and no mistakes made.

06:08.100 --> 06:10.100
Which means they just actually pile up.

06:10.100 --> 06:25.100
But in reality, 80% of what everybody does from a day to day...

06:25.100 --> 06:38.800
Thank you, Mr. Truck.

06:38.800 --> 06:44.720
But in reality, 80% of what most professionals do every single day, it's repetitive tasks.

06:44.720 --> 06:50.240
It's the same thing almost every single day with slight little nuances per each client

06:50.240 --> 06:57.800
or for a new product or for a new feature that you're rolling out for a SaaS service.

06:57.800 --> 07:12.800
And that's exactly where AI becomes your first hire.

07:12.800 --> 07:19.720
If you've run a business for longer than six months, then you know hiring is horrible.

07:19.720 --> 07:20.640
It's time consuming.

07:20.640 --> 07:21.640
It's frustrating.

07:21.640 --> 07:25.640
And you very often train the wrong candidate only having to fire them six months later.

07:25.640 --> 07:32.640
Delegating tasks to them requires hand-holding and repetitive instructions over and over and over until they're actually fully trained and get it.

07:32.640 --> 07:38.560
But with AI, you can actually offload those tasks.

07:38.560 --> 07:44.480
You train them once.

07:44.480 --> 07:46.480
You iterate maybe another one or two times and then it's done.

07:46.480 --> 07:50.400
All of those repetitive tasks, they're just completely and cleanly automated.

07:50.400 --> 07:57.400
So I want you to think of all of those low value tasks, all of those things that you really need to do.

07:57.400 --> 08:01.400
But with AI, you can actually offload those tasks.

08:01.400 --> 08:02.400
You train them once.

08:02.400 --> 08:06.400
You iterate maybe another one or two times and then it's done.

08:06.400 --> 08:11.400
All of those repetitive tasks, they're just completely and cleanly automated.

08:11.400 --> 08:23.400
So I want you to think of all of those low value tasks, all of those things that you really don't want to do that aren't actually money drivers.

08:23.400 --> 08:25.400
How do you automate that?

08:25.400 --> 08:27.400
How do you turn that over to AI?

08:27.400 --> 08:30.400
That AI should be your first hire.

08:30.400 --> 08:37.400
You call it your intake receptionist or whatever it is that role you actually want to have on board.

08:37.400 --> 08:38.400
That was dumb.

08:41.400 --> 09:10.400
Instead of paying someone that you've hired to sort through emails and summarize social media posts or schedule social media posts or send out emails or add things or remove things from your calendar.

09:10.400 --> 09:13.400
AI can actually do all of those repetitive tasks.

09:13.400 --> 09:22.400
And if you have an executive assistant or a front desk receptionist, you can actually have them amplify all of their tasks with AI as well.

09:22.400 --> 09:29.400
So it's not just a replacement of your staff.

09:29.400 --> 09:31.400
It actually enhances everybody on your team.

09:31.400 --> 09:41.400
So if you already have a team, your next hire shouldn't be a new person.

09:41.400 --> 09:47.400
It should be the next AI agent that optimizes everything for most people on your team.

09:47.400 --> 09:55.400
And the best part, once you actually get this all up and rolling, it starts to compound.

09:55.400 --> 09:57.400
It connects all your systems together.

09:57.400 --> 10:00.400
They communicate more seamlessly.

10:00.400 --> 10:02.400
There's less data silos.

10:02.400 --> 10:04.400
There's less information islands.

10:04.400 --> 10:06.400
And everybody is actually on the same plate.

10:06.400 --> 10:08.400
And everybody is on the same page.

10:08.400 --> 10:13.400
Whether it's marketing, sales, rev ops, front desk, you name it.

10:13.400 --> 10:20.400
All of that data starts to get centralized.

10:20.400 --> 10:42.400
These fucking trucks.

10:42.400 --> 10:43.400
Just think about it.

10:43.400 --> 10:49.400
One automation triggers the next.

10:49.400 --> 10:50.400
